  "output": {
    "answer": "There's no platform behind it — it's just conventions written into a file. The end time is one line in the lane brief: run continuously until a named hour, then stop or pause, not \"run overnight.\" Caps are three numbers set before the run starts, also written into the brief so they're visible: a cap on tool calls, one on wall-clock time, one on spend. The morning report is a single file, not a pile of logs — each lane writes its own short report into it, or a coordinator assembles them, so I read one file in the morning instead of chasing logs.",
